chkdsk  
chkdsk C:  
chkdsk C: /f  
chkdsk C: /r  
chkdsk C: /scan  
chkdsk C: /spotfix  
chkdsk C: /f /x

/f Fix errors. Requires exclusive access to the volume.
/r Locate bad sectors and recover readable data. Implies /f. Slow.
/x Force the volume to dismount first. Implies /f.
/scan Online scan of an NTFS volume with no dismount.
/spotfix Apply fixes found by /scan, requiring only brief downtime.
/b Re-evaluate previously flagged bad clusters. Implies /r.
/i Skip thorough index checks. Faster, less complete.
/c Skip directory cycle checks. Faster, less complete.


